{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And He said.</b> For נגש, from the stem of והנוגשים אצים (Exodus 5:13), is a nif'al construction, and the meaning is that he afflicts his soul for nothing, to fast. (A.G. from ויגש אליו יהודה, Genesis 44:18.)" "<b>With their mouth.</b> Each one." "<b>The commandment of men learned by rote.</b> Like the meaning of רגילות, as כעגל לא למד (Jeremiah 31:18)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The abbreviation א\"ג likely denotes אחרים גורסים ('others read'); resolved by inference from the cited variant source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:55.046044329Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}